    "narrative": "The offensive outlook for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the speed-infused profile of **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the squad with a 79.76 score against Roki Sasaki. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup where Sasaki\u2019s deliberate delivery significantly elevates the stolen base probability, bolstered further by a favorable spot in the #2 hole. Similarly, **Brice Turang** (70.40) is a high-priority start today, as his leadoff role combined with a plus-matchup against Matthews creates the perfect environment to attack the base paths. **Mickey Moniak** (68.44) rounds out the top tier of our outfield, deriving a substantial +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Leahy, signaling he is a primary driver for our Roto output this afternoon.\n\nWe are navigating a few tactical hurdles, most notably with **Isaac Paredes** and **Zach McKinstry**, whose projected scores remain in flux as we await official lineup confirmation. **Isaac Paredes** holds a 56.67, benefiting significantly from a high-skill opponent in Ray despite the platoon disadvantage, making him our most viable UTIL play. On the bench, **Cole Young** was the closest to cracking the active roster, but his 35.72 score fell well below our 40-point floor; he struggled to overcome the drag of facing the elite arm of Drew Rasmussen, which ultimately relegated him to the bench in favor of more high-upside plays. With **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** remaining sidelined on the IL, we are closely monitoring the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** to ensure we maintain optimal coverage across our remaining daily game caps.",
